# Performance Best Practices

## React Performance

- Use Server Components by default
- Mark Client Components explicitly with 'use client'
- Implement proper memoization (React.memo, useMemo, useCallback)
- Avoid unnecessary re-renders
- Use key props correctly in lists
- Minimize component tree depth
- Extract static content outside components
- Use proper dependency arrays in hooks

## Code Splitting

- Use dynamic imports for large components
- Implement route-based code splitting
- Lazy load non-critical features
- Use next/dynamic for client components
- Split vendor bundles appropriately
- Analyze bundle size with Next.js Bundle Analyzer
- Minimize initial bundle size
- Load third-party scripts strategically

## Image Optimization

- Always use next/image component
- Set proper width and height attributes
- Use appropriate image formats (WebP, AVIF)
- Implement lazy loading (default in next/image)
- Use proper sizes attribute for responsive images
- Optimize image quality settings
- Use blur placeholders for better UX
- Consider using Supabase Storage with CDN

## Data Fetching

- Use Server Components for data fetching
- Implement proper caching strategies
- Use parallel data fetching when possible
- Minimize waterfall requests
- Implement proper loading states
- Use streaming with Suspense
- Cache frequently accessed data
- Prefetch data when appropriate

## Caching Strategies

- Use appropriate cache headers
- Implement revalidation with revalidatePath/revalidateTag
- Use static generation when possible
- Implement ISR (Incremental Static Regeneration)
- Cache API responses appropriately
- Use CDN for static assets
- Implement browser caching
- Use SWR or React Query for client-side caching

## Database Performance

- Use database indexes effectively
- Minimize database queries
- Implement query optimization
- Use select to fetch only needed fields
- Implement pagination for large datasets
- Use Supabase connection pooling
- Cache database queries when appropriate
- Monitor query performance

## Bundle Optimization

- Minimize bundle size
- Use tree shaking effectively
- Remove unused dependencies
- Use proper import strategies
- Avoid importing entire libraries
- Use barrel exports carefully
- Implement code splitting
- Monitor bundle size in CI/CD

## Font Optimization

- Use next/font for font optimization
- Load fonts from local files when possible
- Minimize font weights and variants
- Use font-display: swap
- Preload critical fonts
- Remove unused font variants
- Consider variable fonts
- Subset fonts when possible

## Third-Party Scripts

- Use next/script component
- Load scripts with appropriate strategy (afterInteractive, lazyOnload)
- Minimize third-party scripts
- Defer non-critical scripts
- Monitor third-party impact on performance
- Consider alternatives to heavy libraries
- Load scripts conditionally
- Use web workers for heavy computation

## CSS Performance

- Use Tailwind CSS purge/content configuration
- Minimize custom CSS
- Extract critical CSS
- Use CSS modules for component styles
- Avoid inline styles when possible
- Minimize CSS specificity
- Use CSS containment when appropriate
- Remove unused Tailwind classes

## Core Web Vitals

- Monitor Largest Contentful Paint (LCP)
- Optimize First Input Delay (FID) / Interaction to Next Paint (INP)
- Minimize Cumulative Layout Shift (CLS)
- Use Lighthouse for performance audits
- Monitor real user metrics (RUM)
- Set performance budgets
- Test on various devices and networks
- Optimize for mobile performance

## Server-Side Performance

- Minimize Server Component computation
- Use edge runtime when appropriate
- Implement proper error boundaries
- Optimize Server Actions
- Use streaming for large responses
- Minimize middleware overhead
- Implement proper rate limiting
- Monitor server performance

## State Management Performance

- Minimize client-side state
- Use proper context splitting
- Avoid unnecessary context re-renders
- Implement proper memo patterns
- Use state selectors effectively
- Minimize prop drilling
- Use Zustand or similar for complex state
- Profile state updates

## Network Performance

- Minimize HTTP requests
- Use HTTP/2 or HTTP/3
- Implement proper compression
- Use CDN for static assets
- Implement resource hints (preconnect, prefetch)
- Minimize payload sizes
- Use proper cache headers
- Optimize API response sizes

## Rendering Performance

- Use Server Components when possible
- Minimize client-side JavaScript
- Implement proper loading strategies
- Use Suspense boundaries appropriately
- Avoid layout thrashing
- Batch DOM updates
- Use requestAnimationFrame for animations
- Minimize paint and composite operations

## Monitoring and Testing

- Use Next.js Analytics
- Implement performance monitoring (Vercel Analytics, Sentry)
- Monitor Core Web Vitals
- Use Lighthouse CI
- Test on real devices
- Monitor bundle size changes
- Set up performance budgets
- Profile with React DevTools

## Mobile Performance

- Optimize for mobile networks
- Test on low-end devices
- Minimize JavaScript execution
- Implement progressive enhancement
- Use proper touch targets
- Optimize for mobile viewports
- Test on various mobile devices
- Consider offline functionality

## Best Practices

- Measure before optimizing
- Focus on user-perceived performance
- Set performance budgets
- Monitor performance in production
- Implement progressive enhancement
- Test on various devices and networks
- Use performance profiling tools
- Document performance optimizations
- Regular performance audits
